  "instruction": {
    "text": "Sort the objects by category into the three baskets.",
    "origin": "task/RoboDojo/tasks/classify_objects.py::gen_instruction"
  },
  "source": {
    "robodojo_revision": "ee67a1468510da7624a089164402359f2afc72c8",
    "assets_revision": "a14409d7fae673c00499e01fd88b4457df6351b1",
    "eval_seed": 0,
    "layout_folder": "Eval_Layout/RoboDojo/arx_x5/0",
    "ordinal_rule": "SeedManager.init_eval (env/seed_manager/seed_manager.py:33-43) sorts <task>_<n>.json numerically; the 55 files are numbered 0-54 without a gap, so ordinal n is <task>_<n>.json"
  },
  "decision": "User decision 2026-10-01: EXP11A g012 adds a three-round session (K = 3 rounds) of classify_objects with a new reviewed layout of eval_seed 0 per round. This appendix extends the classify_objects review-v2 record from layout 0 to the reviewed pool 49, 54, 37 and the fallback 50 without changing its contract text, and binds each audited layout's object metadata.",
  "criteria": [
    "Instruction: gen_instruction (task/RoboDojo/tasks/classify_objects.py:101-103) returns the constant template \"Sort the objects by category into the three baskets.\" with no placeholder, so every layout delivers the reviewed instruction; the worker refuses a round whose upstream instruction differs from round 0.",
    "Objects: every audited layout holds exactly the three Rigid groups cat0, cat1 and cat2 that run_reward reads by label prefix, each of one category with two or three instances, the three categories distinct, and no other Rigid instance. The baskets basket0-basket2 (basket/2, /3, /4) and the camera stand under Geometry, and the Room, Table, Ground and Background sections, are JSON-equal to the reviewed layout 0.",
    "Contract text: the three review-v2 sentences name no category, count, position or model; \"a separate basket for each category\" holds because every audited layout has exactly three categories for the three baskets. The layout-0 categories (pen, watch, garage) are evidence for layout 0 only and are never delivered.",
    "Evaluator: is_all_A_in_B and is_all_A_z_lower_than_B_bbox_zmax read object root poses and each basket's metadata oriented box. The settled check pairs cat_i with basket_i (record review note); the three basket models have the same oriented box (0.252 x 0.168 x 0.077 m), so that pairing acts the same in every layout.",
    "Evaluator assets: the record binds the metadata of every object instance of layout 0 (evaluator_dependencies). Each row binds the metadata of every object instance of its own layout (evaluator_asset_dependencies; the layout-0 row reproduces the record's set byte for byte), which RunSpec resolution discloses for the scheduled layouts and fresh preflight re-hashes with the record's own dependencies (fail closed).",
    "Asset load: action_camera/1 has no physics mass in its layout entries or its asset metadata, so RigidObject (env/scene_manager/objects/rigid.py) loads it at the 0.5 kg default; no audited layout holds it and no audited object is mass-clamped.",
    "Not a reachability review: whether an arm reaches each object is decided by the catalog review (computed spawn distances) and the scene smoke (scheduled_object_reach); fixtures and placement targets are not reach-checked."
  ],
